 last architecture left; and how plastic, bronze sculpture, radio waves, and some man-made molecules may be our most lasting gifts to the universe. As he shows which human devastations are indelible, and which examples of our highest art and culture would endure longest, Weisman's narrative ultimately drives toward a radical but persuasive solution that needn't depend on our demise.--From publisher description."},"latest_revision":28,"revision":28,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2010-03-18T05:06:32.630522"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-07-10T22:38:54.318586"}},{"publishers":["Thomas Dunne Books"],"number_of_pages":336,"ia_box_id":["IA121011"],"weight":"1.2 pounds","covers":[7447786],"physical_format":"Hardcover","last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2016-09-23T13:13:57.767914"},"latest_revision":16,"key":"/books/OL9661439M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL402867A"}],"ocaid":"worldwithoutu00weis","subjects":["Science: General Issues","Science","Environmental Studies","Science/Mathematics","Earth Sciences - General","Environmental Science","Science / Earth Sciences","Effect of human beings on","Human-plant relationships","Material culture","Nature"],"isbn_13":["9780312347291"],"source_records":["amazon:0312347294:2-ap:2427390765:264551","marc:marc_loc_updates/v35.i14.records.utf8:13163895:1257","marc:marc_loc_updates/v35.i15.records.utf8:12844245:1483","marc:marc_loc_updates/v35.i16.records.utf8:16920280:1578","marc:marc_loc_updates/v36.i45.records.utf8:4470954:1627","marc:CollingswoodLibraryMarcDump10-27-2008/Collingswood.out:76628024:2689","marc:marc_ithaca_college/ic_marc.mrc:222730297:1436","ia:worldwithoutu00weis"],"title":"The World Without Us","identifiers":{"goodreads":["248787"],"librarything":["2141148"]},"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-30T09:38:13.731961"},"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"isbn_10":["0312347294"],"publish_date":"July 10, 2007","works":[{"key":"/works/OL2746364W"}],"ty